drm/sun4i: set TCON_TOP_PORT_SEL_REG to 0x20 rather than 0

From ROCKNIX's 0003-Update-sun8i_tcon_top.c.patch, by Philippe Simons, whose
own commit message reads "hack to fix first row on panel".

Upstream status: not upstream, and described by its author as a hack. Kept as
its own patch precisely so it can be dropped in one step.

sun8i_tcon_top_bind() clears TCON_TOP_PORT_SEL_REG on the grounds that some
bits are set by default and cause trouble. On H616 ROCKNIX writes 0x20 there
instead of 0.

Unverified, and worth being explicit about because this register selects which
mixer feeds which TCON -- the same thing the device tree port graph describes.
So this either duplicates the DT routing harmlessly or overrides it. If the
image is shifted by one row, this patch is why; if there is no image at all,
try dropping it before suspecting the DT.
From e455e1333985180431dc6de43d3ab97a2f608edc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2025 22:19:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Update sun8i_tcon_top.c

hack to fix first row on panel
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_tcon_top.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_tcon_top.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_tcon_top.c
index 8adda578c51b..badb6609d8ed 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_tcon_top.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_tcon_top.c
@@ -179,7 +179,7 @@ static int sun8i_tcon_top_bind(struct device *dev, struct device *master,
 	 * At least on H6, some registers have some bits set by default
 	 * which may cause issues. Clear them here.
 	 */
-	writel(0, regs + TCON_TOP_PORT_SEL_REG);
+	writel(0x20, regs + TCON_TOP_PORT_SEL_REG);
 	writel(0, regs + TCON_TOP_GATE_SRC_REG);
 
 	/*
